1
00:00:00,455 --> 00:00:03,392
湖水突然变绿，是谁干的？
The lake has turned green. Who did it?

2
00:00:04,438 --> 00:00:06,748
我叫小藻，先别急着怪我！
I'm Little Alga. Don't blame me just yet!

3
00:00:09,455 --> 00:00:11,597
藻类本来是水里的生产者。
Algae are the water's primary producers.

4
00:00:12,036 --> 00:00:17,045
靠阳光制造食物，释放氧气，还养活浮游动物和鱼类。
They use sunlight to make food, release oxygen, and support the food web.

5
00:00:18,114 --> 00:00:20,881
常说的蓝藻，其实是蓝细菌。
So-called blue-green algae are actually cyanobacteria.

6
00:00:23,455 --> 00:00:27,214
一天，多余的氮和磷随径流进入水里，
One day, runoff brings excess nitrogen and phosphorus into the water.

7
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:29,599
像给小藻送来了一大桌营养。
It's like a nutrient feast for Little Alga.

8
00:00:30,038 --> 00:00:32,871
污水排放，也可能带来这些营养。
Wastewater can bring these nutrients too.

9
00:00:33,949 --> 00:00:34,830
开饭啦！
Time to eat!

10
00:00:36,455 --> 00:00:40,370
再遇上适宜的光照和温度，藻类就可能加快生长。
With suitable light and temperature, algae may grow faster.

11
00:00:40,809 --> 00:00:44,124
但不同的藻，喜欢的条件并不相同。
But different algae thrive under different conditions.

12
00:00:45,189 --> 00:00:48,935
把藻量想成一本账：增加持续超过减少，
Think of an algae budget: when gains keep exceeding losses,

13
00:00:49,022 --> 00:00:50,317
就会越积越多。
algae accumulate.

14
00:00:53,454 --> 00:00:57,087
风和水流，还会把已有的藻推到一起。
Wind and currents can also gather existing algae together.

15
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:00,958
看，数量没变，只是站得更挤了。
Look: the number is unchanged. They're just packed closer.

16
00:01:02,003 --> 00:01:05,894
岸边变绿，不一定等于全湖都长出了新藻。
A green shoreline doesn't always mean more algae across the lake.

17
00:01:07,455 --> 00:01:11,777
当藻类大量增长或聚集，局部浓度明显升高，
When algae grow or gather in large amounts, their local concentration rises.

18
00:01:11,797 --> 00:01:12,804
就是水华。
That's a bloom.

19
00:01:13,243 --> 00:01:15,854
湖泊和海洋里，都可能发生。
It can happen in lakes and oceans alike.

20
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:19,728
但热闹过头，就有麻烦了。
But when the party gets too crowded, trouble follows.

21
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:21,502
藻太多会遮光；
Too many algae block light.

22
00:01:21,682 --> 00:01:25,910
大量藻体死亡后，微生物分解它们，又会消耗氧气。
When masses of algae die, microbes use oxygen to break them down.

23
00:01:26,330 --> 00:01:29,336
即使水变清了，风险也未必结束。
Even when the water clears, the risk may remain.

24
00:01:30,387 --> 00:01:31,883
我快喘不过气了。
I can barely breathe!

25
00:01:33,455 --> 00:01:35,089
还有些种类会产毒。
Some species also produce toxins.

26
00:01:35,501 --> 00:01:38,138
不过，不是每次水华都有毒；
But not every bloom is toxic.

27
00:01:38,395 --> 00:01:40,772
不产毒，也可能造成缺氧。
Non-toxic blooms can still deplete oxygen.

28
00:01:42,455 --> 00:01:43,189
怎么办？
What can we do?

29
00:01:43,615 --> 00:01:47,503
减少多余营养进入水体，保护湿地和岸带，
Reduce nutrient inputs. Protect wetlands and shorelines.

30
00:01:47,604 --> 00:01:51,036
持续监测藻类、氧气和必要的毒素。
Monitor algae, oxygen and, when needed, algal toxins.

31
00:01:54,446 --> 00:01:57,666
目标不是消灭小藻，而是让水里的生活，
The goal isn't to wipe out Little Alga. It's to bring aquatic life

32
00:01:57,686 --> 00:01:58,974
重新保持平衡。
back into balance.
